        "startSec": 1461,
        "endSec": 1705,
        "why": "This clip widens the frame from heaven as a location to the Bible’s story of reunion. It says that “heaven and earth were unified in the Garden of Eden,” that resurrection is “bound up with…new creation,” and that Jesus embodies God’s presence while announcing that “the kingdom of God…has arrived.”",
        "episodeTitle": "When Heaven Meets Earth",
        "sourceId": "bibleproject",
        "source": "BibleProject",
        "audioUrl": "https://afp-597195-injected.calisto.simplecastaudio.com/695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee/episodes/6e13ef8a-244f-41e8-bf58-dfd0c94e1798/audio/128/default.mp3?awCollectionId=695767b0-cd40-4e6c-ac8c-ac6bc0df77ee&awEpisodeId=6e13ef8a-244f-41e8-bf58-dfd0c94e1798",
        "durationSec": 2213,
        "adInsertionDrift": false
      },
      {
        "recordId": "bibleproject:podcast:heaven-earth-q-r",
        "startSec": 641,
        "endSec": 814,
        "why": "Now pause over the question of what happens between death and resurrection. The speakers discuss Jesus’ promise, “Today you’ll be with me in paradise,” Paul’s language of being “with Jesus,” and the honest limit that “the Bible just doesn’t talk about” most details of the intermediate state.",
        "episodeTitle": "Heaven & Earth Question & Response",
